{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore"},{"type":"text","text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size, until they are delivered."}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let store = try SegmentStore(events: [SignedUp.self, CheckedOut.self])","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)"]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Write-through."}]},{"text":" A tracker’s worker writes each record as it reaches it, before publishing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it, with one ","type":"text"},{"code":"write()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", off the tracking caller’s thread, so the record survives the app","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"crashing or being killed from then on. The store makes the log durable against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"power loss too (","type":"text"},{"code":"fsync","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") once per batch, before the batch is delivered, and whenever","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is called: call it, after the tracker’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as the app moves to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"background or terminates.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A record whose write fails (the disk is full, say) is kept in memory only, and reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What is kept."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Only events of the types in ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which conform to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/BinaryCodable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Events of any other type are kept in memory only: they are delivered in this run like any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other, are never written, and produce no drop report, but are lost if the app ends first.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A record’s context is not kept: a recovered record is in the top-level ","type":"text"},{"code":"ServiceContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as its span ended with the earlier run.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Deleting."}]},{"type":"text","text":" A segment is deleted as a whole once every record in it is delivered, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"log whose records are all delivered holds no files. There is no compaction: a segment kept"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for one undelivered record keeps its delivered ones too."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Bound."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The log never holds more than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"byteBound"},{"type":"text","text":" bytes. When a record wouldn’t fit, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"oldest segments are deleted until it does, and each one deleted with records not yet"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered yields a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". A record too large for an empty log"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is kept in memory only."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Recovery.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" A store opened on a directory recovers the records earlier runs left there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and a tracker given the store delivers them first. Each segment is cut at its first torn or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"corrupt record, keeping every intact record before it, and the bytes cut off are reported.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A segment comes back whole, delivered records and all. Each record a delivery had started on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comes back with ","type":"text"},{"code":"isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" set, as it may have reached a destination already: one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered before the app ended, or one delivered just as it ended, before the store could","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delete its segment. A record whose delivery mark can’t be written is held back from that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivery, so it is never sent twice unannounced, and delivered on a later launch.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Other versions.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" A segment a newer release of the app wrote, in a later version of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format, is left on disk untouched after a rollback, for that release to deliver: this one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neither reads it nor counts it toward the bound. A segment in an earlier version, which this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one can’t read, is deleted and reported as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/corruption(byteCount:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Changed event types."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Each record’s event is a map of its properties by name, so a record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written before its type changed still reads: a property removed since is skipped, an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"optional one added since is ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and one with a default value added since has it. A record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stored at another ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event.schemaVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" than its type’s now is dropped without being read and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reported as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"One at the same version that can’t be read all the same, after a required property was added","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or a property’s type changed without raising the version, is dropped and reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Open one store per directory at a time; two would delete each other’s segments. Copies of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store share its log."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/byteCount","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/directory","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/pendingRecordCount"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/append(_:)","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","